CORE
shared-loop-variable1.sv
--bound 0
^\[main\.p0\] always main\.a == main\.din: REFUTED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^file .* line \d+: `Verilog::\$root\.main\.i' has multiple drivers$
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
A module-level 'integer' loop counter shared by two clocked always
blocks must not be reported as a driver conflict during RTL
construction. verilog_rtl_buildert::commit (src/verilog/verilog_rtl.cpp)
used to track writes to every symbol assigned in an always block,
including elaboration-only 'integer' loop counters, and rejected a
counter shared by two blocks as a spurious driver conflict. The same
exemption that verilog_synthesist::assignment_rec applies (PR #2049) is
now also applied in the verilog_rtl.cpp builder used here.
